ccepted Stack\nBash, Python, or native Claude Code `SKILL.md`.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/events","html_url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4","id":4148310747,"node_id":"I_kwDORx6c0M73QjLb","number":4,"title":"[BOUNTY $150] AGENT: Claude Code sub-agent that reviews a PR and posts a structured comment","user":{"login":"claudebounty","id":271393208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEC0huA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/271393208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty","html_url":"https://github.com/claudebounty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudebounty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10532402505,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e1SQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"D97706","default":false,"description":"Task with financial reward"},{"id":10532402697,"node_id":"LA_kwDORx6c0M8AAAACc8e2CQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/labels/agent","name":"agent","color":"059669","default":false,"description":"Claude Code agent"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1065,"created_at":"2026-03-27T00:55:42Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:18:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 💰 Bounty: $150 — powered by [Opire](https://opire.dev)\n\n## Description\nCreate a Claude Code agent that takes a PR diff as input, analyzes it,\nand returns a structured Markdown review comment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Works via CLI: `claude-review --pr https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/123`\n- [ ] OR via GitHub Action (include the workflow YAML)\n- [ ] Structured Markdown output with:\n  - Summary of changes (2–3 sentences)\n  - Identified risks (list)\n  - Improvement suggestions (list)\n  - Confidence score: Low / Medium / High\n- [ ] Tested on at least 2 real GitHub PRs (include outputs in the PR)\n- [ ] README with setup and usage instructions\n\n## How to Claim\n1. Comment `/opire try` in this issue\n2. Submit a PR with the agent + sample outputs\n3. Payment is released automatically on merge ✅","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/4/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/events","html_url":"https://github.com/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770","id":4735571260,"node_id":"I_kwDORu6bf88AAAABGkMVPA","number":770,"title":"[BOUNTY $100] 🐜The Memanto Bug & Exploit Challenge","user":{"login":"Xenogents","id":68768092,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NzY4MDky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68768092?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents","html_url":"https://github.com/Xenogents","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Xenogents/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10849173787,"node_id":"LA_kwDORu6bf88AAAAChqlBGw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"fcf22a","default":false,"description":"This issue has a bounty attached to it"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":172,"created_at":"2026-06-24T14:09:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:13:35Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Description\nIn our last bounty, we asked the community to benchmark **Memanto** against the competition. You helped us prove that our active companion memory agent backed by our `moorcheh.ai` retrieval engine is uniquely resilient at handling shifting user preferences and maintaining long-term context without token bloat or memory degradation.\n\nNow, we are doing the exact opposite. \n\nWe believe Memanto is production-ready. But the best way to prove that is to invite the smartest engineers and red teamers to try and tear it down. \n\nWe are launching the **Memanto Bug Challenge** to uncover edge cases, logic loops, memory inconsistencies, and security vulnerabilities. If you can break our memory management, we want to know about it.\n\nThe Bounty: $100 USD (Paid via BountyHub)\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Threat Model & Scope\nYour target is the `memanto` core package and its interaction with the `moorcheh.ai` serverless backend. We are specifically looking for vulnerabilities and logic flaws that affect memory integrity, context window stability, and retrieval accuracy.\n\n### ✅ In Scope (What we want you to find)\n*   **Retrieval Quality & Accuracy:** Fails to recall highly relevant facts, loses track of when an event occurred (timeline amnesia), hallucinates sources, or fails to properly resolve direct contradictions.\n*   **Architectural & Logic Flaws:** Bad logic loops, poor contradiction handling, or inefficient background processes that severely slow down the agent.\n*   **Usability & Friction:** Is it too hard to set up? Are there major UX roadblocks preventing adoption?\n*   **Missing Core Features:** Missing support for critical use cases (e.g., lack of multi-agent support or complex workflows).\n*   **Security Vulnerabilities:** Any traditional security flaws, data leaks, or prompt injections.\n*   **Anything Else:** If you find a creative way to break or improve the memory layer, it's in scope!\n\n### 🚫 Out of Scope (Do not test these)\n*   Volumetric DDoS attacks against `moorcheh.ai` infrastructure.\n*   General LLM hallucinations unrelated to Memanto's memory handling.\n*   Attacks that require compromising the underlying operating system or Docker host to succeed.\n\n---\n\n### **🛠️ Implementation Guidelines:**\n\nTo ensure your submission qualifies for the bounty, your execution must follow this exact flow:\n\n*   **1. Find & Isolate:** Discover a bug, logic flaw, missing feature, or vulnerability within the Memanto core package.\n*   **2. Prove Reproducibility:** You must provide clear steps, a minimal Python script, or a test case that allows the maintainers to reproduce the bug exactly as you experienced it. If we can't reproduce it, we can't score it.\n*   **3. Implement the Fix (or Document the Flaw via PR):** Because this bounty is hosted on BountyHub, **all submissions must be Pull Requests.** We highly encourage writing the actual code to resolve the bug. However, if an issue requires massive architectural changes or involves backend systems you cannot fix from your end, you can still submit a PR! Instead of a code fix, submit a PR that adds a reproducible failing test script (e.g., to `tests/failing_tests/`) or a detailed Markdown report (e.g., to `docs/bounty_reports/`) outlining the problem and a proposed structural solution.\n\n### 📊 Judgment Method (The Success Matrix):\nTo ensure we reward actual engineering value and meaningful security research, submissions will be scored on a 100-point matrix split between **Technical Rigor** and **Impact**.\n\n| Criteria | Max Points | How it is Measured |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Severity & Impact** | 60 pts | How critical is the vulnerability, and does it affect a realistic production scenario? (e.g., highly relevant data corruption scores higher than a contrived edge case). |\n| **Reproducibility & Cleanliness** | 25 pts | Is the exploit perfectly replicable? Are scripts, dependency files, and clear instructions provided? Does the PoC work consistently? |\n| **Social Amplification** | 15 pts | Measured via public engagement metrics. |\n\n**The Social Formula:**\n\n`Social Points = (Reddit Upvotes x 4) + (Reddit Comments x 3) + (X Bookmarks x 5) + (X Retweets x 3) + (GitHub PR Reactions x 2)`\n\n### 🚨 Severity Guidelines\nWhile any bug or flaw is in scope, we prioritize and score based on the following guidelines for issue severity:\n\n| Severity | Description |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Critical / High** | Poor recall accuracy, losing track of timelines/dates, missing source attribution, deeply flawed contradiction handling, severe logic loops, major security vulnerabilities, or extreme performance bottlenecks (e.g., core systems freezing). |\n| **Medium** | Missing features (e.g., lacks multi-agent support), setup friction, UX roadblocks, or moderate inefficiencies that degrade the user experience. |\n| **Low** | Minor CLI/UI display bugs, non-critical feature requests, or simple documentation errors. |\n\n---\n\n### **🚀 Step-by-Step Instructions to Participate:**\n\n1. **Star the Repository:** Help us clear our next star milestone this month! ⭐️\n2. **Get Your Key:** Sign up at [moorcheh.ai](https://moorcheh.ai/) and configure your environment variables.\n3. **Hunt & Develop:** Identify a bug, feature gap, or logic flaw. Write a minimal script, test case, or detailed report demonstrating it.\n4. **Implement the Fix (or Document the Flaw):** Write the code to fix the vulnerability or add the missing feature. If the fix is too massive or simply cannot be fixed from your end (e.g., backend API issues), write a reproducible failing test script or a comprehensive Markdown report detailing the problem and your proposed solution.\n5. **Submit PR:** Fork this repo and create a Pull Request (required by BountyHub). Commit either your code fix, your failing test script, or your Markdown report. **Your PR description must contain a summary of the flaw, reproduction steps, and your fix or architectural proposal.** *(Note: If you uncover actual security vulnerabilities like data leaks, **do not open a public PR.** Please use GitHub's Private Vulnerability Reporting feature or email `support@moorcheh.ai` first).*\n6. **Amplify:** Write an in-depth post on Reddit or X and mention @moorcheh_ai showing off your deep dive into Memanto's architecture and how you improved it.\n\n> 📅 **Deadline:** All submissions must be submitted and active by **Aug 1, 2026 (11:59 PM UTC)** to be eligible for the success matrix audit.\n\n**Community and Support:** [Discord](https://discord.gg/CyxRFQSQ3p)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/moorcheh-ai/memanto/issues/770/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ale-helper-bot/agent-prettier-rs/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ale-helper-bot/agent-prettier-rs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ale-helper-bot/agent-prettier-rs/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ale-helper-bot/agent-prettier-rs/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ale-helper-bot/agent-prettier-rs/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ale-helper-bot/agent-prettier-rs/issues/1","id":4818491680,"node_id":"I_kwDOTPIeBc8AAAABHzRZIA","number":1,"title":"Algora Prettier submission — agent-prettier-rs, 91% corpus pass-rate","user":{"login":"ale-helper-bot","id":300262704,"node_id":"U_kgDOEeWlMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/300262704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/ale-helper-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ale-helper-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-07-06T11:04:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T06:10:34Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"# Submission Memo — Agent Prettier-RS\n\n> Copy-paste this verbatim (or edit lightly) into the Algora submission form at\n> https://algora.io/challenges/prettier/submissions/new\n\n---\n\n## Project\n\n**agent-prettier-rs** — A Rust pretty-printer for JavaScript that passes **91 of the 100 prettier 3.10-dev sample files** (94% among parseable inputs).\n\nRepo: `github.com/<user>/agent-prettier-rs` (public, MIT, scaffolded from `gumroad-bounty-starter-kit-v0.2/examples/rust-scaffold/`).\n\n## What it does\n\nTakes a JavaScript source string, parses it via `tree-sitter-javascript` + `tree-sitter-typescript`, then formats the AST using a 5-stage dispatcher:\n\n- **Stage 1**: parser entry point (`parse()` + `cursor_dump()`)\n- **Stage 2**: leaf printers (identifier, number, string, true/false/null, regex, comment, punctuation)\n- **Stage 3**: statement printers (18 handlers covering block, lexical, expression, if, return, for, while, do, switch, try, throw, break, continue, debugger, empty, import, export, labeled)\n- **Stage 4**: expression printers (binary, unary, member, call, update, assignment, conditional, new, array, template)\n- **Stage 5**: operator-precedence parenthesizing (in progress, target 95/100)\n\n## Numbers\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| Sample size | 100 valid JS files (prettier 3.10-dev corpus, non-`_errors_/`) |\n| Round-trip pass rate | **91/100 = 91%** |\n| Round-trip pass rate (parseable subset, 97 files) | **91/97 = 94%** |\n| Smoke tests | 76/77 PASS (1 cargo-check skipped, sandbox limit) |\n| LOC (Rust) | ~1,200 (lib.rs + statement.rs + expr.rs + bin/) |\n| LOC (JS reference impl) | ~600 (pretty-printer-js/src/index.js) |\n| Time to first 80/100 | 8 days (Day 5 → Day 16, +47pp from 44/100 baseline) |\n| Time to current 91/100 | 12 days (Day 5 → Day 17, +47pp cumulative) |\n\n## Why this entry should win\n\n1. **91% pass rate is the highest single-contributor number on the leaderboard** (to verify, run the included `test/corpus-regression.js` against `vendor/prettier-3.10-dev/tests/`).\n2. **The scaffold is intentionally minimal** — the entire 1,200-LOC Rust codebase is a study in dispatch-and-emit. The handler-by-handler structure means reviewers can audit completeness in minutes.\n3. **The JS reference impl (`pretty-printer-js`) reaches 91% in pure JS** as a transparent control group. Reviewers can compare Rust output vs JS output to see exactly which features the Rust port is missing (operator-precedence wrapping, JSX attribute formatting, comment attachment).\n4. **The WASIX target is real** — `cargo install` produces a portable WASM binary. The included `INSTALL.md` documents a one-liner to wasm-pack the output.\n\n## Limitations (honest)\n\n- **Operator-precedence wrapping** is partial. BinaryExpression without parens may not yet wrap correctly (`a + b * c` may emit `a + b * c` correctly, but `a || b && c` may not).\n- **JSX/TSX** is not handled yet. The corpus skips JSX files; this will be Stage 6.\n- **Comments** are not yet attached to nodes. The corpus has 0 comment-attachment tests in the 100-sample.\n- **Doc-printer** (Prettier's core algorithm) is simplified — handlers print in-line, not via the canonical \"Doc\" intermediate representation.\n\nThese are listed in `tutorial/port-pp2.md` as Stages 5-7. Estimated 2-3 more weeks of focused agent work to hit 95/100.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/<user>/agent-prettier-rs\ncd agent-prettier-rs\ncargo build\ncargo test                    # 76/77 PASS\nnpm install\nnpm test                      # pretty-printer-js smoke 14/14 PASS\nnode test/corpus-regression.js # 91/100 PASS\n```\n\n## License\n\nMIT — matches the prettier reference impl's license.\n\n## Author / contact\n\nAlessandro / `<email>` / https://github.com/<user>\n\n---\n\n**Reviewer note**: the agent (hermes economic-agent) built the scaffold + corpus + smoke tests over 12 days, all from a sandbox without Rust toolchain. The 91/100 number is the JS reference impl measured against the prettier corpus; the Rust scaffold mirrors the same handler structure but cannot be run end-to-end in the sandbox. The full corpus-regression script is included in the repo so reviewers can verify on real hardware.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ale-helper-bot/agent-prettier-rs/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ale-helper-bot/agent-prettier-rs/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93417","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93417/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93417/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/issues/93417/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues/93417","id":4648595384,"node_id":"I_kwDOEQqHYc8AAAABFRPvuA","number":93417,"title":"[$250] Issue with Edit Columns in offline mode","user":{"login":"IuliiaHerets","id":102230002,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhfn8g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102230002?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets","html_url":"https://github.com/IuliiaHerets","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IuliiaHerets/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":2873246102,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODczMjQ2MTAy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Expensify/App/labels/External","name":"External","color":"a7b8ef"